 {parms}←CheckErrorFolder parms;buff;qdmx
⍝ Establishes `parms.errorFolder` as a full path and creates the folder if it does not exist and
⍝ `checkErrorFolder` is 1. A folder that cannot be created is recorded as a problem; see `AddProblem`.\\
⍝ Returns `parms`.
 :If 0=≢parms.errorFolder
     buff←AppName ⎕WSID
     :If 'Win'≡APLTreeUtils2.GetOperatingSystem ⍬
         parms.errorFolder←(2 ⎕NQ'.' 'GetEnvironment' 'LOCALAPPDATA'),'/',buff,'\Errors'
     :Else
         parms.errorFolder←FilesAndDirs.PWD,'/Errors'
     :EndIf
 :EndIf
 parms.errorFolder←{(-(¯1↑⍵)∊'/\')↓⍵}FilesAndDirs.NormalizePath parms.errorFolder
 :If 0=+/'/\'∊parms.errorFolder
     parms.errorFolder←FilesAndDirs.NormalizePath FilesAndDirs.PWD,'/',parms.errorFolder
 :EndIf
 :If 0=⎕NEXISTS parms.errorFolder
 :AndIf parms.checkErrorFolder
     :Trap parms.trapInternalErrors/0
         3 ⎕MKDIR parms.errorFolder
     :Else
         qdmx←⎕DMX
         parms←('The error folder could not be created: ',qdmx.EM,(0<≢qdmx.Message)/': ',qdmx.Message)AddProblem parms
     :EndTrap
 :EndIf
